.TH QUIPU-STORE 1 "" quipu "Quipu Manual"
.SH NAME
quipu\-store \- Inspect native ownership, or explicitly adopt or restore a disk store
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquipu store\fR [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect native ownership, or explicitly adopt or restore a disk store
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Store file (default: .bobbin/quipu/quipu.db; configuration may override it)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
quipu\-store\-status(1)
Report inactive or enforced native store ownership without adopting
.TP
quipu\-store\-adopt(1)
Bind an existing native store to this host and path with a fresh epoch
.TP
quipu\-store\-restore(1)
Restore a SQLite snapshot to a new path and explicitly adopt it
.TP
quipu\-store\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
